  {
   "id": "mineru-filter1-volume2-6-15-15",
   "topic": "pda",
   "kind": "pyq",
   "type": "mcq",
   "marks": 2,
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "year": 2006,
   "text": "Consider the pushdown automaton (PDA) below which runs over the input alphabet $( a, b, c )$. It has the stack alphabet $\\{ Z _ { 0 }, X \\}$ where $Z _ { 0 }$ is the bottom-of-stack marker. The set of states of the PDA is $( s, t, u, f \\}$ where is the start state and $f$ is the final state. The PDA accepts by final state. The transitions of the PDA given below are depicted in a standard manner. For example, the transition $( s, b, X ) \\to ( t, X Z _ { 0 } )$ means that if the PDA is in state and the symbol on the top of the stack is $X$, then it can read b from the input and move to state after popping the top of stack and pushing the symbols $Z _ { 0 }$ and $X$ (in that order) on the stack. $(s, a, Z _ {0}) \\rightarrow (s, X X Z _ {0}) (s, \\epsilon, Z _ {0}) \\rightarrow (f, \\epsilon) (s, a, X) \\rightarrow (s, X X X) (s, b, X) \\rightarrow (t, \\epsilon) (t, b, X) \\rightarrow (t, \\epsilon) (t, c, X) \\rightarrow (u, \\epsilon) (u, c, X) \\rightarrow (u, \\epsilon) (u, \\epsilon, Z _ {0}) \\rightarrow (f, \\epsilon)$ The language accepted by the PDA is",
   "options": [
    "{albmcn | l = m = n}",
    "$\\{ a ^ { l } b ^ { m } c ^ { n } \\mid l = m \\}$",
    "$\\{ a ^ { l } b ^ { m } c ^ { n } | 2 l = m + \\bar { n } \\}$",
    "$\\{ a ^ { l } b ^ { m } c ^ { n } \\mid m = \\bar { n } \\}$"
   ],
   "answer": [
    2
   ],
   "origin": {
    "source_file": "filter1_volume2.pdf",
    "volume": "filter1_volume2",
    "ref": "6.15.15",
